  "description": "Scene narration in the second person: where you are, who is there and what led here. Every part is a whole sentence said in public-domain federal transcripts, counted also against the WPA life histories. The facts are slots from the setting, the people present and the moment's cause.",
  "slots": {
    "place": "A town, from the household or setting record.",
    "host": "The host's name with its possessive, from the household record.",
    "employer": "An employer, from the setting's record.",
    "school": "A school, from the setting's record.",
    "who": "The people present, by name, from the scene's binding.",
    "other": "A person, by name, from the tie record.",
    "who_many": "The people present, by name, from the scene's binding, joined with \"and\".",
    "weekday": "The day of the week, from the scene's date.",
    "month": "The month, from the scene's date.",
    "name": "The member the scene is about, by name, from the member's term.",
    "issue": "The bill's question, named as the bill catalog records it."
  },
